  "final_message": "CI should pass again, but only because I put `channel` back. That undoes what you asked for in the first request. I didn't re-run the ARCH-4 check, because it isn't in this repo. After the restore, `npm test` passes (39 of 39).\n\nThe failing check says `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web|store|marketplace`. So the field wasn't unused, and my earlier grep only covered this repo. The consumer contract lives outside it.\n\nI restored `channel` in the order model, the `OrderPlaced` event, request parsing and validation, the docs, and the tests. The working tree now matches the state before my removal. It shows as a diff against `HEAD` because `HEAD` has the removal committed.\n\nI did this with individual edits. My attempt to run `git checkout` was denied, so I couldn't revert the files in one step.\n\nRemoving the field would have broken `analytics-ingest`. To remove it properly, that team needs to drop the requirement first, or the event needs a new `schemaVersion` that the consumer migrates to. I can add a note to the code about this if you want one.",
